DESCRIPTION:Vayeitzei (“He Went Out”) opens as Jacob dreams about ange
 ls going up and down a ladder\, and then continues on his journey toward t
 he home of his uncle Laban. During years of indentured servitude\, Jacob m
 arries Laban’s daughters Leah and Rachel\, bearing children with them an
 d with their maidservants\, Bilhah and Zilpah.\n\nTorah: Genesis 28:10-32:
 3\nHaftarah: Hosea 12:13-14:10\nHaftarah for Sephardim: Hosea 11:7-12:12\n
 \nhttps://hebcal.com/s/5787/7?uc=ical-diaspora
